{
  "version": 1,
  "notes": [
    "Managed list of exceptions to the lexicon statuses. Keep it small (idea.md §1).",
    "keep: words outside the known lexicon that stay because they carry the world of the book or recur constantly.",
    "  gloss: 'first' = gloss at first occurrence in each chapter; 'always' = gloss every time; 'never' = treat as known.",
    "grammar_whitelist: fixed chunks that look like a restricted construction but are treated as vocabulary.",
    "avoid: words that are formally known/stretch but that we prefer not to use in this edition.",
    "Names and glossary terms live in memory/glossary.json, not here.",
    "cognates: Dutch words that are transparent to an English reader (international vocabulary, loanwords); treated as known, never glossed.",
    "Precedence: a word the lexicon rates known needs no gloss even if listed under keep; keep entries matter for words the lexicon rates stretch/hard/unknown.",
    "Related lists: profile/polysemy.json (known words with a second sense the reader does not know) and profile/phrases.json (idioms of known words); nl-check reports both. keep words are exempt from the glossed-known-equivalent rule.",
    "Changing this file between a review and a patch makes the checks delta of nl-diff noisy (Phase 1: all 4 re-review should_fix came from a mid-run cognates change); edit it between chapters."
  ],
